    "q-196452": {
      "dom_id": "step-q196452",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Roy, Kate, and Connor divided $\\frac{1}{3}$ of a watermelon equally among themselves. What part of a watermelon did each of the $3$ friends get?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, each of the friends got \n{{field-1}} of a watermelon.",
      "worked_solution": "To determine the part of the watermelon each friend got, we must divide the amount of watermelon by the number of friends.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷3\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷3=\\frac{1}{3\\times 3}=\\frac{1}{9}\n$$\n\nTherefore, each of the $3$ friends got $\\frac{1}{9}$ of a watermelon.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
