    "q-91869": {
      "dom_id": "step-q91869",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Peter prepares $\\frac{1}{3}$ of a liter of coffee to distribute, in equal quantities, to his $5$ guests. How much coffee will each guest receive?",
      "worked_solution": "To find out how much coffee each guest will receive, we have to divide the amount of coffee by the number of guests:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷5\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷5=\\frac{1}{3\\times 5}=\\frac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nTherefore, each guest will receive $\\frac{1}{15}$ liters of coffee.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
