    "q-196453": {
      "dom_id": "step-q196453",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Zoe distributed $\\frac{1}{2}$ kilograms of sausage equally between $4$ cats. How much sausage did each cat receive?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, each cat received\n{{field-1}}  kilograms of sausage.",
      "worked_solution": "To determine the amount of sausage per cat, we must divide the amount of sausage by the number of cats.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷4\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷4=\\frac{1}{2\\times 4}=\\frac{1}{8}\n$$\n\nTherefore, each cat received $\\frac{1}{8}$  kilograms of sausage.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
