      "dom_id": "step-q196454",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "A farmer divided his field into $3$ smaller lots of equal area. What is the area of each lot if the total area of the field is $\\frac{1}{2}$ acres?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, the area of each lot is\n{{field-1}} acres.",
      "worked_solution": "To determine the area of each lot, we divide the total field area by the number of lots.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷3\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷3=\\frac{1}{2\\times 3}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of each lot is $\\frac{1}{6}$ acres.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
